[00:17.00]inland a. 内陆的，内地的‖ad. 在内陆，向内地 示例 ① There have been plans for nuclear plants inland, cooled by rivers, but concerns about the availability of water in drier years to come and the risk of contaminating it may cause these plans to be shelved. 曾有过在内地建造利用江河进行冷却的核电站的计划，但是对旱年冷却水可能会出现短缺以及核电站可能会造成水污染的担忧也许是这些计划最终没有落实的原因。（The Economist）② This company is mainly dealing with inland trades. 这家公司主要从事国内贸易。
[00:26.21]prevalent a. 普遍存在的，流行的，盛行的 示例 ① Newspapers relay daily accounts of goal-setting prevalent in industries and businesses up and down both Wall Street and Main Street, yet there has been surprisingly little research on how the long-trumpeted practice of setting goals may have contributed to the current economic crisis, and unethical behaviour in general. 报纸上每天都充斥着关于华尔街或主街上各行各业制定业绩目标的报道。然而令人惊讶的是，但是对于这些长期被吹捧的目标设定行为可能加剧当前的经济危机和整体上的不道德行为这一点，相关研究却寥寥无几。（2012. 6）② The use of robots are increasingly prevalent in recent years. 近几年，机器人的应用越来越普遍。
[00:35.93]witness n. 目击者；证人；证词；证明‖v. 当场见到，目击 示例 ① The witness was told that under no circumstances should he lie to the court. 目击证人被告知任何情况下都不许对法庭有不实之词。（2007. 12）② We are privileged to witness a major breakthrough in astronomy. 我们有幸见证航空领域的重大突破。 语料 Life without a friend is death without a witness. 人生没有朋友犹如死亡无人见证。
[00:42.93]gaze n. & v. 凝视，注视 示例 ① Millions looked skyward Sunday to gaze upon the spectacular light show known as the annular solar eclipse, where the moon passes in front of the sun, leaving only a bright ring of light.周日，数百万人仰望天空，凝视着被称为环形日食的华丽的光秀——月亮从太阳前面经过，只留下明亮的光环。（Time）② She gazed at me in disbelief when I told her the news. 我告诉她这消息时，她以怀疑的目光注视着我。
[00:49.79]furthermore ad. 此外，而且 示例 ① Furthermore, by gauging the reactions to our self-disclosures we learn what types are acceptable or unacceptable with particular people and in specific situations. 此外，通过测量自我表露的反应，我们得知与特定的人和在特殊的情况下，哪些类型是可以接受的，哪些类型是不可接受的。（2012. 12）② Furthermore, Google is tiptoeing into the country with only a handful of services. 此外，谷歌只提供了很有限的服务就悄悄地进入了这个国家的市场。
[00:58.65]ascend v. 上升，升高；登高；向上延伸 示例 ① In 1970, after a Conservative general election victory, she ascended to the Ministry of Education. 1970年，她在保守党大选中获胜，升任教育部部长。（The Washington Post）② The path started to ascend more steeply. 小径开始陡峭向上。
[01:04.96]correlate v. 相互关联或影响，相互依赖；显示紧密联系 示例 ① At its most straightforward, a green neighbourhood simply means more places for kids to play—which is vital since time spent outdoors is one of the strongest correlates of children's activity levels. 最直接的一点是，绿色社区最起码意味着孩子们有更多的玩耍空间——这是至关重要的，因为在户外的时间是与孩子们活动水平最直接相关的因素之一。（2010. 6）② The figures do not seem to correlate. 这些数字似乎毫不相干。
[01:13.61]stumble v. 绊脚；跌跌撞撞地走；结结巴巴地说话‖n. 绊脚；出错 示例 ① It is more of a haphazard stumble, and then a dawning sense of opportunity that is seized upon by those destined to become entrepreneurs. 更多的是一次偶然的失足，然后开始看到一线机会，而那些注定成为企业家的人抓住了这个机会。（Financial Times） ② Any man may stumble into crime when among criminals. 同犯罪分子混在一起，任何人都可能失足犯罪。
[01:20.07]vitamin n. 维生素 示例 ① There are many nutrients that are thought to be potentially protective for cancer, including vitamin D, selenium, carotenoids, other antioxidants, and specific fatty acids. 有很多营养素被认为有潜在抗癌的功效，包括：维生素D、硒、类胡萝卜素、其他一些抗氧化剂和一些特定的脂肪酸。（New Scientist）② Vitamin pills make up what we lack in our diet. 维生素片可以弥补我们饮食中的不足。
[01:27.80]asset n. 资产，财产；有价值的特性或技能， 优点 示例 ① Imagine waking up and finding the value of your assets has been halved. 想象一下有一天醒来你发现自己的资产价值缩减了一半。（2008. 6）② In his job, patience is an invaluable asset. 对于他所从事的工作，耐心是无价之宝。
[01:33.57]update vt. 使现代化；更新；向…提供最新信息‖n. 更新 示例 ① So in October 1915 Einstein threw himself into a month-long frantic endeavor in which he returned to an earlier mathematical strategy and wrestled with equations, proofs, corrections and updates that he rushed to give as lectures to Berlin's Prussian Academy of Sciences on four successive Thursdays. 所以在1915年10月，爱因斯坦进行了一个月的疯狂努力。他回到早些时候的数学策略，着力于方程式、证明、修改和更新，心急地连续四个星期四在柏林普鲁士科学院做讲座。（2007. 12）② Information and knowledge in this field update very fast. 这个领域的信息和知识更新得很快。
[01:43.52]decorate v. 装饰；点缀；粉刷 示例 ① Even in France, where the government rejects talk of "austerity" or public-sector pay cuts, the political elite is doing its bit: the education minister is reported to have started to decorate his offices with artificial flowers. 甚至在法国， 尽管政府拒绝谈论“财政紧缩”或是削减公共部门工资，政治精英们也尽力而为：有报道说教育部长已经开始使用假花来装饰他的办公室。（The Economist）② The country decorated the soldier for bravery. 国家表彰了这名士兵的英勇行为。
[01:51.02]disguise v. 假扮；掩饰‖n. 伪装行为；伪装物 示例 ① In "UNDERCOVER BOSS", a British television programme, company chiefs disguise themselves and work on the shop floor of their own companies. The climax comes when the boss reveals his true identity to his co-workers. Much to his surprise, the shop-floor grunts often have no clue who he is. 英国有一档电视节目叫“卧底老板”，公司老板乔装打扮后，下到自己公司一线与员工一起工作。当老板向一起工作的员工揭开自己的真实身份时，节目达到高潮。让老板感到十分吃惊的是，这些基层员工常常不知道自己的老板是谁。（The Economist）② He tries to disguise his real feelings. 他试图掩饰自己的真实情感。
[01:58.74]suicide n. 自杀 示例 ① According to the presentation, more teens die in automobile crashes in the United States each year than from drugs, violence, smoking and suicide. 根据描述，在美国，每年死于交通事故的青少年要比死于吸毒、暴力、吸烟和自杀的青少年多。（2009. 6）② Smoking is chronic suicide. 吸烟等于慢性自杀。
[02:04.76]parliament n. 国会；议会 示例 ① Back in 1989 Parliament unanimously supported a resolution to eliminate child poverty by 2000. 早在1989 年（加拿大）议会就全体一致通过一项决议，支持在2000年前消除儿童贫困。（The Economist）② The parliament has the right of passing a law. 议会有权制定法律。
[02:10.31]opponent n. 对手；反对者 示例 ① Several opponents have recently emerged, ranging from rival tech giants such as Microsoft and Amazon to small bodies representing authors and publishers across the world. 最近世界各地涌现出一些反对者，包括谷歌的竞争对手， 如微软和亚马逊这些科技巨头，也包括代表作者和出版商的小机构。（2011. 12）② He bowled out his opponent. 他打败了他的对手。
[02:17.00]election n. 选举，推选（尤指从政）；当选 示例 ① As Erin White watched the election results head towards victory for Barack Obama, she felt a burden lifting from her shoulders. 当埃琳•怀特看到大选结果倾向于巴拉克•奥巴马获胜时，她感觉肩上的负担卸了下来。（2010. 6）② There is no doubt but that he will win the election. 毫无疑问他会在竞选中获胜。
[02:23.41]species n. 种，物种；类型 示例 ① A report by the Fish and Wildlife Service showed a worrisome drop in the populations of several species of North Atlantic sea turtles, notably loggerheads, which can grow to as much as 400 pounds. 渔业和野生动物署的一份报告表明，几种北大西洋海龟的数量急剧下降，这令人担忧，尤其是体重能够长到400磅的红海龟。（2009. 6）② We should do our best to save endangered species. 我们应该竭尽全力拯救濒临灭绝的生物。
[02:31.68]innate a. 天生的，先天的，固有的，天赋的 示例 ① But most importantly, he shares with Mr. Jobs an innate understanding of the importance of thinking about high-tech products from the customer's point of view. 但最重要的是，他和乔布斯一样生来就了解从顾客的角度来思考高科技产品的重要性。（The Economist）② I believe everyone have an innate sense of self-respect. 我认为每个人都有一种与生俱来的自尊心。
[02:38.27]enrol v. 登记，招收，记入名册 示例 ① This fall, 16 first-year students and four second-year students at Hartwick enrolled in the school's new three-year degree program. 今年秋天，哈特威克学院有16名大一新生和4名大二学生报名参加该校新的三年制学位课程。（2012. 6）② They enrol him as a member of the club. 他们将他吸纳为俱乐部成员。
[02:44.44]awkward a. 棘手的；笨拙的 示例 ① Einstein also took time off from furiously revising his equations to engage in an awkward fandango with his competitor Hilbert. 在近乎疯狂地修改他的方程式期间，爱因斯坦还抽出一部分时间和他的竞争对手希尔伯特尴尬地胡闹。（2007. 12）② You dealt with an awkward situation very tactfully. 你很巧妙地处理了一个尴尬的局面。
[02:50.99]substantial a. 大量的；牢固的 示例 ① And yet there are substantial sectors of the vast U.S. economy—from giant companies like Coca-Cola to mom-and-pop restaurant operators in Miami— for which the weak dollar is most excellent news. 但对于庞大美国经济中大量的产业部门——从可口可乐这样的大公司到迈阿密的夫妻餐厅经营者——美元疲软的消息对他们来说可是再好不过了。（2008. 6） ② The man is fifty years old and does not have a substantial job. 那个男人都50岁了还没有一份正经工作。
[02:59.93]fibre n. 纤维；纤维素；纤维制品 示例 ① These days, for high-end bikes where weight is at a premium, they turn to aluminium alloys or even to carbon fibre. 如今，对高端自行车来说，车身重量是溢价的部分，他们借助于铝合金甚至是碳纤维。（The Economist）② Green vegetables contain more fibre than other foods. 绿色蔬菜比其他食物纤维含量高。
[03:06.16]dilemma n.（进退两难的）窘境，困境 示例 ① Mr. Reshef's university has yet to win accreditation, which could take years. But he can take comfort from Clayton Christensen's classic book "The Innovator's Dilemma". 里谢夫先生的大学目前还在办理资格认证，这可能会耗时数年。 不过，他能够从克莱顿•克里斯坦森的经典大作《创新者的窘境》中获取慰藉。（The Economist）② She was in a dilemma whether to go to see him or not. 她不知道该不该去见他。
[03:16.21]haul v. （用力）拖，拉；强迫（某人）去某处‖n. 拖，拉 示例 ① Hauling the branches to the front for garbage pick-up was no fun either. 将树枝拖到前院垃圾回收处也很费事。（2006. 12）② We hauled on the boat up the beach. 我们用力拖小船，把它拖到了沙滩上。
[03:20.66]ultimate a. 最终的；根本的，基本的‖n. 最好的事物 示例 ① This might seem like the ultimate defeat for racism, but ignoring the race of certain select individuals—a phenomenon that psychologists call subtyping—also has an insidious side. 这看上去像是种族主义的终极胜利，但是，忽略某些特定个体的种族——心理学家将这种现象称为“亚归类” ——也有其自身的隐患。（2010. 6）② He said it is still not possible to predict the ultimate outcome. 他说现在还不可能预测最终的结果。
[03:28.41]odour n. 气味（尤指不好的气味） 示例 ① He helped set up the International Society for Breath Odour Research in 1995. 1995年，他帮助成立了国际呼吸气味研究学会。（New Scientist）② The foul odour penetrated the entire house. 整个房间都弥漫着难闻的臭气。
[03:33.16]consensus n. 意见一致，共识 示例 ① Yet the consensus among most economists is that immigration, both legal and illegal, provides a small net boost to the economy. 然而，大多数经济学家们的共识是，不管是合法移民还是非法移民，都对经济起到了少许的促进作用。（2011. 6）② There is a general consensus among us about building a harmonious society. 我们对建立一个和谐的社会有着普遍的共识。
[03:44.33]odd a. 奇数的；奇怪的；不成对的；非固定的‖n. 怪人；怪事；剩余物 示例 ① Self-honoring or self-love may seem like an odd step for job hunters, but being to accept yourself, without judgment, helps eliminate insecurities and will make you more self-assured. 自我尊重和自我热爱对求职者来说可能是奇怪的一步，但毫无批判地接受自己有助于消除不安全感，会使你更自信。（2007. 6）② The odd thing was that he was avoiding her. 怪就怪在他躲着她。
[03:51.35]electrical a. 电的，用电的，发电的 示例 ① Human brains rely on electrical impulses to release calcium ions that bind to neurotransmitters that, in turn, communicate with the rest of the nervous system. 人脑依赖电脉冲来释放钙离子，这些钙离子绑定于神经传导素，反过来，神经传导素又与其他神经系统相连。（The Economist）② There is an electrical fault in the engine. 发动机出现了电气故障。
[03:56.65]instance n. 例子，事例‖v. 举…为例 示例 ① For instance, why does it have to take four years to earn a diploma? 例如， 为什么必须花费四年来获得一个文凭？（2012. 6）② What should you do, for instance, if you are caught in a big fire? 例如，当你被困在大火中时，你应该怎么办？
[04:03.59]immune a. 有免疫力的；不受影响的；免除的 示例 ① In the past five years it has become clear that the immune system often prevents tumours by identifying and eliminating malignant cells at an early stage of development. 在过去的五年里，免疫系统在癌症早期通过识别和消灭癌细胞控制肿瘤生长已变得明晰起来。（The Economist）② I seem to be immune to colds and flu. 我似乎对感冒和流感免疫。
[04:10.75]primitive a. 原始的；简陋的‖n. 原始派画家 示例 ① As they report in Nature, the critter, which lived around 55m years ago, in the Eocene epoch, seems to be the most primitive relative of tarsiers, mouse-sized primates which now inhabit the islands of South-East Asia. 正如他们发表在《自然》杂志上的文章所述，这种生活在大约五千五百万年前新世时期的生物似乎是眼镜猴最原始的亲戚。眼镜猴是一种体型很小的灵长类动物，现居住在东南亚的岛屿上。（The Economist）② It is a primitive instinct to escape from a place of danger. 逃离危险的地方是一种原始本能。
[04:18.82]sophisticated a. (人)老于世故的；高雅时髦的；（物）复杂的，精良的；尖端的 示例 ① The newer trend is to start recruiting poor and non-white students as early as the seventh grade, using innovative tools to identify kids with sophisticated verbal skills. 最新的趋势是， 在7年级时就开始录取穷学生和非白人学生， 并运用创新的方式识别那些有精湛语言表达能力的孩子。（2011. 6）② She has become very sophisticated since she went to live abroad. 移居国外后她变得特别世故。
[04:26.46]religious a. 宗教的；虔诚的 示例 ① Students may choose among 6,000 public, private, nonprofit, for-profit, or religious institutions of higher learning. 学生可以在6000所公立、私立、非营利、营利或宗教性的高等院校中进行选择。（2012. 6）② All of us were very religious and felt it was a gift from God. 我们都很虔诚，并且感觉它是上帝的恩赐。
[04:34.90]badge n. 徽章；标记，象征 示例 ① He served in the U.S. Army where he was awarded the Presidential Service Badge. 他曾在美国军队服役，被授予总统服务徽章。（The New York Times）② The olive leaf is a badge of peace. 橄榄叶是和平的象征。
[04:39.25]deviate v. 偏离，背离 示例 ① The schools so established are free to vary the lengths of the school day and year, and to deviate both from the national curriculum and from the national pay structures for teachers. 这些学校可以自主制定每天和每学年的课时数，也可不必同公立学校统一的课程安排及教师的薪酬体系保持一致。（The Economist）② She always deviates from what she is talking about when making a class presentation. 在做课堂展示时，她总会背离她谈论的主题。
[04:48.02]balance v. 使保持平衡；权衡‖n. 天平，秤；平衡 示例 ① Its parent company, the New York Times Company, has 15 papers, but suffered a loss of $70 million in the nine months to September and recently accepted a $250 million loan from a Mexican billionaire, Carlos Slim, to strengthen its balance sheet. 其母公司纽约时报公司，旗下发行15份报纸，但到九月份的九个月间损失了7000万美元。最近，纽约时报公司接受了墨西哥亿万富翁卡洛斯•斯利姆提供的一笔2500万美元的贷款以巩固其财务状况。（2010. 12）② You'd better check the balance in your account. 你最好查一下账户余额。
[04:55.46]repel v. 击退，驱逐；使厌恶，使反感；推开，赶走；拒绝 示例 ① Other Antwerp schools banned scarves on the ground of equality but in reality, says Ms Azabar, they wanted to repel pupils from poor backgrounds who might pull them down academic league tables. 阿扎巴尔说，安特卫普的其他学校以平等之名禁止在校内戴头巾，但实际是想把那些出身贫寒的学生赶出去，因为他们会拉低学校在学术榜上的排名。（The Economist）② I was repelled by the smell of gasoline. 汽油的气味让我恶心。 语料 Like poles repel each other. 同极相斥。
[05:02.88]democratic a. 民主的；（D-）（美国）民主党的 示例 ① American scholars fanned out across much of the world—with support from the Ford Foundation, the Fulbright program, etc.—to promote the teaching of literature and the arts in an effort to make the case for democratic freedoms. 在福特基金、富布莱特项目等的资助下，美国学者在世界大部分地区散布开来，促进文学和文科的教育，以充分彰显民主自由。（2010. 12）② Freedom of speech prized above all others in a democratic society. 在民主社会，言论自由高于其他一切权利。
